  <UserdefinedSymbols/>
  <LuaScript>--[[
TITILE:     GTA:SAN_ANDREAS Cheats App (".exe")
Author:     TKBS
INFO:       A Companion App for ".pnach" cheats.
            + A basic template for creating cheat apps with CE.
ISSUE 1:
  Screen == PRIMARY Monitor, not the actual window we hooked
  ... which makes no sense coz we hook and anchor text to it.
  that text font size is set based on primary monitor (in my case - 1080p)
  so if we switch midgame to a 4k monitor, text is way too samll.

ISSUE 2:
  CE checks and unchecks boxes randomly - be careful to spot this
  CE Saves the state of boxes etc irrelevant of the code so if you test something then save itll save that state.

ISSUE 3,4,5:
  * Timers may be an issue (resource intensive)
  * ampersand symbols not supported ?
  * I cannot use dynamic addresses or pointers so my work-around with AOB is a bit convoluted.

ISSUE 6:
  * The following code crashes but it is needed to make sure when app loads any incorrect vehicle IDs are set to a valid one.

  if VHIDSHOW1 &gt; 611 then
  VHIDSHOW1 = 611
  end

  if VHIDSHOW1 &lt; 400 then
  VHIDSHOW1 = 400
  end

